    "source_id": "issue:7044",
    "repository": "streamlit/streamlit",
    "body": "### Checklist\n\n\n### Summary\n\nWhen using a key to create a data editor it throws the following error:\r\n`\r\nStreamlitAPIException: Values for st.button, st.download_button, st.file_uploader, st.data_editor and st.form cannot be set using st.session_state.\r\n`\r\n\r\nWhen removing the key, the error disappears.\n\n### Reproducible Code Example\n\n```Python\nWith key:\r\n\r\n`\r\nst.data_editor(\r\n    data=companies_df,\r\n    key='companies_df',\r\n    disabled=True,\r\n    hide_index=True,\r\n    height=500,\r\n    use_container_width=True,\r\n    column_config={\r\n        'name': st.column_config.TextColumn(width=100),\r\n        'ticker': st.column_config.TextColumn(width=25),\r\n        'exchange': st.column_config.TextColumn(width=25),\r\n        'score': st.column_config.ProgressColumn(width=100),\r\n        'description': st.column_config.TextColumn(width=100),\r\n        'url': st.column_config.LinkColumn(width=100),\r\n    },\r\n)\r\n`\r\n\r\nWithout key\r\n`\r\nst.data_editor(\r\n    data=companies_df,\r\n    disabled=True,\r\n    hide_index=True,\r\n    height=500,\r\n    use_container_width=True,\r\n    column_config={\r\n        'name': st.column_config.TextColumn(width=100),\r\n        'ticker': st.column_config.TextColumn(width=25),\r\n        'exchange': st.column_config.TextColumn(width=25),\r\n        'score': st.column_config.ProgressColumn(width=100),\r\n        'description': st.column_config.TextColumn(width=100),\r\n        'url': st.column_config.LinkColumn(width=100),\r\n    },\r\n)\r\n`\n```\n\n\n### Steps To Reproduce\n\n_No response_\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nApp should work with key\n\n### Current Behavior\n\nThrows error when using key\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\n- [ ] Yes, this used to work in a previous version.\n\n### Debug info\n\n- Streamlit version: 1.23.1\r\n- Python version: 3.9\r\n- Operating System: Ubuntu 20.04 / WSL2\r\n- Browser: Chrome\r\n\n\n### Additional Information\n\nTested both on local and on Streamlit cloud",
